<BlogPost slug="prime-iptv-trial-test">
  <div class="callout"><p><strong>Who wrote this:</strong> we are Prime IPTV, so this is our own service. This is a first-party test by our team, not an independent review. We publish what worked and what did not, and we say what we did not test. The best proof is your own test: the <a href="/free-trial/">24-hour free trial</a> needs no credit card.</p></div>

  <p>We ran a short session on the 24-hour Prime IPTV free trial and wrote down what we saw. Below are the conditions, the results, the problems we found and what we did not test. It is one tester and one session, so treat it as a snapshot, not a guarantee.</p>

  <h2>Test conditions</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Detail</th><th>What we used</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Access</strong></td><td>The 24-hour free trial, no paid purchase</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Server</strong></td><td>The premium server</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Internet speed</strong></td><td>About 60 Mbps</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Time of day</strong></td><td>Peak viewing hours</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Devices and apps</strong></td><td>The app supplied with the subscription, TiviMate and IBO Player on a TV, and an IPTV app on an iPhone. See <a href="/blog/prime-iptv-apps-tested/">the apps we tested</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Length</strong></td><td>One short session, one tester. The exact test date was not recorded; this write-up is dated 29 October 2026.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What we saw</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>Trial login</strong></td><td>Arrived within about 15 minutes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Live TV</strong></td><td>A sample of 98 channels played with no failures.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Sports</strong></td><td>67 sports channels and live sports worked. We did not record which leagues and events.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Streaming at peak hours</strong></td><td>No buffering and no failed channels in the session, at about 60 Mbps.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Movies and series</strong></td><td>The library is 120,000+ titles. Playback worked and search was excellent.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Apps</strong></td><td>All the apps we tried worked without problems.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Support</strong></td><td>Replies came from people on WhatsApp and by email, and the communication was clear and helpful. We did not record response times.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Money-back guarantee</strong></td><td>7 days if there is an issue. See the <a href="/refund/">refund policy</a>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>What did not work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The TV guide (EPG) was only partly working.</strong> It loaded, but it was not complete or reliable in our session. See <a href="/blog/iptv-epg-explained/">how the TV guide works</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Catch-up TV did not work.</strong> Our site says catch-up depends on the player you use, and in our test it did not work.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If a working guide or catch-up matters to you, test them first in your trial, on the player you plan to use.</p>

  <h2>What we did not test</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>4K playback and the resolution of individual channels</li>
    <li>Paid checkout, billing and renewal</li>
    <li>More than one connection at the same time</li>
    <li>The other server options</li>
    <li>Reliability over several days or weeks, and big live events</li>
    <li>The money-back process in practice</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What this means for you</h2>
  <p>In our session the channels, sports and library worked well at peak hours, the apps we tried worked, and support was human and helpful. The guide and catch-up were the weak spots. Your result depends on your device, your player and your connection, so repeat the test yourself with our <a href="/blog/iptv-free-trial-checklist/">24-hour trial checklist</a>.</p>

  <h2>Quick answers</h2>
  <h3>Is this an independent review?</h3>
  <p>No. We run Prime IPTV, so this is our own test of our own service. We wrote down the problems as well as the good results so you can judge it.</p>
  <h3>How many channels did you test?</h3>
  <p>A sample of 98, with no failures, including 67 sports channels. We did not count the full 25,000+.</p>
  <h3>Does Prime IPTV have catch-up?</h3>
  <p>Catch-up depends on your player. It did not work in our test, so check it in your trial if you need it.</p>
  <h3>What internet speed did you use?</h3>
  <p>About 60 Mbps. No speed guarantees good streaming on its own, so test on your own connection.</p>
</BlogPost>
